<p>She gives me this look. This calm, patient, I-know-something-you-don't look that sends a chill down my spine for reasons I can't articulate. "Sure, babe."</p>

<p>We watch a movie. She's fine. Perfectly fine. But there's a degree of warmth missing, like someone turned the thermostat down by two degrees. Not cold. Just... less warm. She sits a little farther away. Her hand stays on her own knee. When I try to put my arm around her, she lets me, but she doesn't melt into it the way she usually does. She just exists next to me, pleasant and present and ever so slightly out of reach.</p>

